---
import Chests42 from '../components/Chests42.astro';
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import ChestDiagram from '../components/ChestDiagram.astro';
import Bars from '../components/Bars.astro';
import Marks from '../components/Marks.astro';
import SizeCompare from '../components/SizeCompare.astro';
import WorkBand from '../components/WorkBand.astro';
import LabLink from '../components/LabLink.astro';
import { LAB } from '../config';
---
<Base title="The evidence: one virtual trial on 42 scanned chests" description="One virtual trial of the device on 42 real, scanned chests: what was compared, what was planned in advance, and what it found.">

<section class="band band-night phero-night" aria-labelledby="h-page">
  <div class="wrap">
    <p class="chip">The evidence</p>
    <div class="score">
      <div class="score-n"><h1 id="h-page" class="numeral"><span class="sr">The evidence: </span>42</h1><Chests42 /></div>
      <div class="score-side">
        <p class="score-line">real chests, scanned. One virtual trial of the device on every one of them.</p>
        <div class="actions"><a class="btn btn-white" href="#method">How the trial works</a></div>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="specs" data-r>
      <div class="spec"><b>25</b><span>women in the set</span></div>
      <div class="spec"><b>17</b><span>men in the set</span></div>
      <div class="spec"><b>21<small>to</small> 59</b><span>years of age, median 53</span></div>
      <div class="spec"><b>1</b><span>heart model, with the same settings in every chest</span></div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="band" id="method" aria-labelledby="h-method">
  <div class="wrap split split-wide-text">
    <div class="split-media frame frame-flush" data-r>
      <ChestDiagram variant="body" alt="The front of a chest outlined from a scan: skin, breastbone, ribs and the heart behind them, with the device on the lower breastbone and its two arms reaching to each side." />
    </div>
    <div class="split-text" data-r>
      <p class="chip">How the trial works</p>
      <h2 id="h-method" class="h2">Real anatomy.<span class="teal">One heart model.</span></h2>
      <p class="lead">Each chest shape comes from a CT scan. The same heart model, with the same settings, beats in every one.</p>
      <ul class="ticks">
        <li>Real chest shapes from CT scans</li>
        <li>The same heart settings in every chest, so the differences come from anatomy</li>
        <li>The sensor rests on the skin under its own footprint</li>
        <li>Four results written down in advance. One was supported: size</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="band band-mist" aria-labelledby="h-size">
  <div class="wrap split">
    <div class="split-text" data-r>
      <p class="chip">Finding one: size</p>
      <h2 id="h-size" class="h2">Small sits<span class="teal">closer.</span></h2>
      <p class="lead">A small stiff core sits closer to the chest than a bank-card-sized one.</p>
      <p>Of the four results written down in advance, this is the one the trial supported. The gaps were measured on the 42 scans.</p>
      <div class="stats">
        <div class="stat"><b>4.45<small>mm</small></b><span>largest gap under the 32 x 60 mm core</span></div>
        <div class="stat stat-dim"><b>9.50<small>mm</small></b><span>under an 86 x 54 mm plate</span></div>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="split-media" data-r>
      <div class="panel panel-wide"><SizeCompare /></div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="band" aria-labelledby="h-place">
  <div class="wrap split">
    <div class="split-media" data-r>
      <div class="panel">
        <p class="panel-k">Beats for the recovery wave, typical chest, by place worn</p>
        <Bars class="bars-big" label="Beats needed by place worn in the trial on 42 chests: 39.9 at the breastbone (the midline spot), 99.5 at the left chest pocket, 106.9 under the left breast." rows={[{ label: 'Breastbone, midline spot', value: 39.9 }, { label: 'Chest pocket', value: 99.5 }, { label: 'Under left breast', value: 106.9 }]} />
        <p class="panel-cap">Six-sensor core, virtual trial on 42 scanned chests.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="split-text" data-r>
      <p class="chip">Finding two: place</p>
      <h2 id="h-place" class="h2">The breastbone<span class="teal">needs fewer beats.</span></h2>
      <p class="lead">In the trial, the breastbone needs fewer beats than the chest pocket or under the left breast.</p>
      <p>The same spot was chosen in 39 of 42 rounds when each chest was left out in turn. At that spot, each left-out chest needed 1.84 times the beats of its own best spot. The limit set in advance was 1.5. The chosen spot is stable; one position does not suit every chest equally.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="band band-tint" aria-labelledby="h-fit">
  <div class="wrap">
    <header class="sec-head" data-r>
      <p class="chip">Finding three: fit</p>
      <h2 id="h-fit" class="h2">A zone,<span class="teal">not a point.</span></h2>
      <p class="lead">The trial on 42 chests chose a spot 3 cm above where the breastbone stops, in the middle of the chest, and showed how much room there is around it. The zone was found after the results were seen, so it is exploratory and not one of the four planned results. The second run then tested it, and the device is now centred at the tested spot: 2 cm above and 2 cm to the wearer's left.</p>
    </header>
    <p class="note" data-r>Measured from the midline spot.</p>
    <div class="tiles tiles-4">
      <article class="tile" data-r><span class="tile-n">3 cm</span><h3>To the wearer's left</h3><p>Beats rise by less than 25 %.</p></article>
      <article class="tile" data-r><span class="tile-n">1 cm</span><h3>Up</h3><p>Beats rise by less than 25 %.</p></article>
      <article class="tile" data-r><span class="tile-n">2 cm</span><h3>Down</h3><p>Beats rise by less than 25 %.</p></article>
      <article class="tile" data-r><span class="tile-n">1.4 x</span><h3>To the right</h3><p>1 cm to the right costs 1.4 times the beats.</p></article>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="band" aria-labelledby="h-next">
  <div class="wrap know">
    <div class="know-head" data-r>
      <p class="chip">The second run</p>
      <h2 id="h-next" class="h2">More chests.<span class="teal">Older chests.</span></h2>
      <p class="lead">A second run on 84 older chests is complete. Two results were written down in advance, and the run supported both. The two runs together hold 126 chests, ages 21 to 94. The plan is to publish them as an open set.</p>
      <div class="actions"><LabLink href={LAB.method}>Sources and method</LabLink></div>
      <p class="note">Opens Sensor exploration, the research tool that holds the sources.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="know-cards">
      <div class="kcard" data-r>
        <p class="kcard-n">42</p>
        <Marks n={42} women={25} label="42 scanned chests: 25 women shown as circles, 17 men shown as squares." />
        <h3>Chests in the trial</h3>
        <p>25 women and 17 men, aged 21 to 59.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="kcard" data-r>
        <p class="kcard-n">84</p>
        <Marks n={84} women={40} label="84 older chests: 40 women shown as circles, 44 men shown as squares." />
        <h3>Older chests, second run</h3>
        <p>40 women and 44 men, aged 61 to 94.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
  <div class="wrap second-run">
    <div class="tiles tiles-4">
      <article class="tile" data-r><span class="tile-n">1.16 x</span><h3>At the tested spot</h3><p>2 cm to the wearer's left and 2 cm above where the breastbone stops, a typical chest needs 1.16 times the beats of its own best spot. The limit set in advance was 1.5.</p></article>
      <article class="tile" data-r><span class="tile-n">74 of 84</span><h3>Better than the midline</h3><p>In 74 of 84 chests that spot needs fewer beats than the midline spot 3 cm above.</p></article>
      <article class="tile" data-r><span class="tile-n">1.48 x</span><h3>Across the zone</h3><p>From the midline to 3 cm left, 2 to 3 cm above: 1.48 times the beats at the zone's middle position. The limit was 1.5.</p></article>
      <article class="tile" data-r><span class="tile-n">0.81</span><h3>Kept per centimetre of depth</h3><p>The main spike falls as the heart lies deeper: 0.81 of it is kept for each extra centimetre between skin and heart.</p></article>
    </div>
    <p class="note" data-r>A third expectation was not supported: that the link with depth grows stronger as a larger area is read. After a known defect of the heart model was repaired, the run was computed again on 83 chests: 1.16, 1.49 and 0.79, with the same three verdicts.</p>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="band band-mist" aria-labelledby="h-more">
  <div class="wrap">
    <header class="sec-head" data-r>
      <p class="chip">Beyond the trial</p>
      <h2 id="h-more" class="h2">Three more reasons<span class="teal">to record both.</span></h2>
    </header>
    <div class="tiles">
      <article class="tile" data-r>
        <p class="tile-k">Hospital study, 202 patients</p>
        <h3>68.4% against 40.5%.</h3>
        <p>In patients with suspected coronary disease, a magnetic heart test found 68.4% of the disease. Exercise ECG found 40.5%. <a class="textlink" href="https://doi.org/10.3233/CH-180485" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Shin and colleagues, 2019</a></p>
      </article>
      <article class="tile" data-r>
        <p class="tile-k">Real recording, modelled electrode failure</p>
        <h3>20 of 20 beats.</h3>
        <p>After a modelled electrode failure on a real recording, the ECG detector found 11 of 20 beats. From the magnetic signal, all 20 were found. The recording is a published one: both signals from one person, taken with a laboratory magnetometer in a shielded room.</p>
      </article>
      <article class="tile" data-r>
        <p class="tile-k">Published by another group</p>
        <h3>Forty adults, no shielded room.</h3>
        <p>Magnetoresistive sensors, the kind the device uses, have recorded the heartbeats of 40 adults in an ordinary room, with 42 sensors and 21 reference sensors. A sensor built round a 4.2 by 2.2 mm chip of this kind has been reported at 4.8 pT per root hertz at 1 Hz.</p>
      </article>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="band band-night" aria-labelledby="h-vow">
  <div class="wrap">
    <p id="h-vow" class="vow vow-top" data-r>We'll make the claim when the evidence does.</p>
    <div class="actions vow-actions" data-r>
      <LabLink class="btn btn-white" href={LAB.trust}>Every check, pass or fail</LabLink>
      <a class="onteal-link" href="/heart-twin/">How the Heart Twin works</a>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<WorkBand />
</Base>
